od  businesses to improve their hygiene  standards the scheme was developed by  the Food Standards Agency and has been  adopted by other local councils such as  south end and basildon there are six  tiers of the scheme ranging from naught  which means urgent improvement necessary  to five very good the businesses that  have been given a rating are cafes  sandwich shops pubs restaurants  supermarkets and other food retailers  certain premises are exempt which  include roll low risk premises not  generally recognized as food businesses  childminders are also exempt as  inspection businesses are rated on three  elements how hygienic Li the food is  handled prepared cooked cooled reheated  and stored the condition of the  structure of the premises cleanliness  lighting and ventilation how the  business manages and records what it  does to make sure food is safe these  three elements are then calculated to  result in a food hygiene rating the  ratings are then displayed on the  website in addition the businesses have  been given a certificate and window  sticker to display at the premises  speaking at the launch in February  Rochford District Council's portfolio  holder for the environment councillor  Mike steptoe said wherever you want to  eat out you will now be able to find a  wealth of information at the touch of a  button rochford District Council is  looking forward to being part of the  scheme and I'm especially pleased to say  that ninety percent of our  establishments received one of the top 3  ratings  Catriona Stewart head of the food  hygiene ratings team that the FSA said  we are encouraging as many local  authorities as possible to run the  scheme so it's great news that Rochford  District Council are the latest to  announce their intention to use it  around 1 million people suffer from food  poisoning every year and our aim in  introducing the scheme is to reduce this  the ratings will give consumers a  glimpse of what is going on in the  kitchen when they